# Local Agent Configurations and Logs. Antigravity's state lives here and is
# none of our business -- except the two things that are deliberately shared.
# `.agents/*` and not `.agents/`: git does not descend into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so a negation for a file inside one is never even considered.
.agents/*
# AGENTS.md and skills/ are the cross-agent instruction layer: the same files
# Claude and Antigravity are both pointed at, so the rules cannot drift apart
# per agent. They were tracked before `.agents/` was ignored, which hid the
# problem -- gitignore does not affect files already in the index, so existing
# skills kept working while a NEW one was silently invisible to `git add`.
# Found the third time that happened in one session (DT-259).
!.agents/AGENTS.md
!.agents/skills/
!.agents/skills/**

# Local Claude Code state (worktrees, scheduled tasks, checkpoints, etc.).
# settings.json is the one exception: it is the shared permission allowlist
# and denylist, so it has to ship with the repo -- a tool other people can
# use safely is the whole point (Boss's rule 4). Personal overrides belong in
# settings.local.json, which stays ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# Local scratch. Dockerfile used to be listed here as "simulation config, do
# not commit" -- DT-228 made it a deliverable (it is how the pinned install is
# verified), and the stale rule silently kept it out of #114 while the PR
# described it in detail. Found by DT-259's own test failing in CI.
scratch_*.py
not_use/

# Generated by `drunken-config --kind install` from uv.lock. Regenerable,
# and committing it would put a second source of truth beside the lock.
requirements.lock.txt
